# What must never enter the production image.
#
# The Dockerfile copies explicitly -- `COPY app/`, `COPY data/`, `COPY main.py`
# -- rather than `COPY . .`, so most of the repository is already excluded by
# construction. This file exists for the one path that is not: `COPY data/
# ./data/` takes the whole directory, and `data/synthetic/generated/` holds the
# training datasets and the Arm A embedding cache. That is roughly 40MB of JSONL
# and 215MB of cached vectors after a five-fold sweep, git-ignored but present
# on the machine of anyone who has run the generator. A local `docker build`
# would bake all of it into an image that serves forms.
#
# Everything here is offline encoder-training output. None of it is read by
# anything under `app/` -- `tests/test_wiring.py` asserts that the dependency
# runs one way -- so excluding it cannot break the running application.

# Generated training datasets, their .stats.json sidecars, and the Arm A
# embedding cache.
data/synthetic/generated/

# Trained heads, metadata sidecars and Arm B's ~440MB-per-fold encoders.
# Belt and braces: the Dockerfile never copies this directory today, and if a
# future `COPY . .` arrives it should not be how 2.2GB of weights ships.
models/

# The evaluation reports. Same reasoning: offline output, no runtime consumer.
reports/

# Local build and tooling noise that only grows the build context.
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
